-- title:
--   Reducedness of algebras generated by the anemic weight-two Hecke algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $N \ge 1$ and let $S$ be a set of natural numbers such that every prime $q$ dividing $N$ belongs to $S$. Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative integral domain of characteristic zero, and let $T$ be a commutative ring equipped with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra structure which is finite and free as an $\mathcal{O}$-module. Write $\mathbb{T} =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) for the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}\bigl(S_2(\Gamma_0(N))\bigr)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ (`heckeTLin`) for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators $U_q$ (`heckeULin`) for primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$; under the hypothesis on $S$ the latter family is empty, so $\mathbb{T}$ is the anemic Hecke algebra generated by the $T_\ell$ with $\ell \notin S$. Assume given a ring homomorphism $\pi \colon \mathbb{T} \to T$ whose image generates $T$ as an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, that is, $\mathcal{O}[\pi(\mathbb{T})] = T$. Then $T$ is reduced: its only nilpotent element is $0$.
--
--   This is the standard reducedness input for weight-two Hecke algebras: away from the primes in $S$ the operators $T_\ell$ act semisimply on $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$, so the anemic Hecke algebra is reduced with $\mathbb{Q}$-étale generic fibre, and reducedness passes to any finite free algebra over a characteristic-zero domain generated by its image. It is used in the construction of the Galois representations attached to local factors of Hecke algebras, where it feeds the identification of Hecke eigenvalues with traces of Frobenius.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_isReduced_of_adjoin_range_heckeAlgebra_eq_top.lean

